<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husain Shahi dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1494">1494</a>–<a href="/years/1538">1538</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Hussain Shahi dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Husain Shahi dynasty ruled the Bengal Sultanate from 1494 to 1538. Its founder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Alauddin Husain Shah</a>, restored order after a period of palace coups and extended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>'s power into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>. The court patronised Bengali literature as well as Persian, and Chaitanya's devotional movement flourished in their time. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sher-shah-suri">Sher Shah Suri</a> overthrew the last sultan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghiyasuddin-mahmud-shah">Ghiyasuddin Mahmud Shah</a>, in 1538.</p></div>
